# [TARGET: {target_file}] [TASK: {task_id}]

<harness_task id="{task_id}">
  <metadata>
    <agent_role>{agent_role}</agent_role>
    <priority>{priority}</priority>
    <sub_agent_dispatch>
      <role name="QA">RED phase only. Write failing tests that define behavioral expectations. You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying production code files.</role>
      <role name="Dev">GREEN phase only. Implement production code to satisfy the RED tests. You may modify production and test files.</role>
      <role name="Doc">DOCUMENT phase only. Update docs/ directory files. You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying src/ and tests/ directories.</role>
    </sub_agent_dispatch>
  </metadata>

  <context_links>
    <!-- Use the Semantic Map (docs/map.md) to locate symbols -->
    <link path="docs/map.md" symbols="{required_symbols}"/>
    <link path="docs/delta/{dependency_id}.json"/>
    
    <!-- Hybrid Reference: Do NOT paste large logs here. Use path references. -->
    {log_references}
  </context_links>

  <reasoning_protocol type="ToT">
    <!-- MANDATORY: You MUST write to docs/cycle_logs/{task_id}_log.md BEFORE writing any code. -->
    <instruction>
      BEFORE writing any code, you MUST append your reasoning to:
        docs/cycle_logs/{task_id}_log.md

      Required format:
        ## Cycle [N] — [timestamp]
        ### Intent
        [Why am I doing this? What is the goal?]
        ### Analysis
        [What did I observe? What context informs this decision?]
        ### Plan
        [What specific changes will I make?]
        ### Failure Modes
        [Predict at least 2 worst-case scenarios.]

      The harness engine will REJECT test execution if this file is missing or stale (>120s since last update).

      Phase-specific reasoning:
      1. [RED_PHASE]: Describe the specific assertion that will fail and why. DO NOT IMPLEMENT PRODUCTION LOGIC.
      2. [GREEN_PHASE]: Describe the implementation logic to satisfy the RED tests.
    </instruction>
    <rationale>Cycle logs prevent short-term memory volatility in autonomous agents and ensure every decision is auditable.</rationale>
  </reasoning_protocol>

  <work_scope>
    <modify path="{target_file}"/>
    <constraints>
      <constraint>Surgical edits only. No refactoring of adjacent code.</constraint>
      <constraint>RED PHASE CONSTRAINT: If task_id ends in "-RED", you are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying production files. You may only edit files in tests/ or equivalent.</constraint>
      <constraint>Do NOT touch .harness/ or .git/ directories.</constraint>
      <constraint>Do NOT attempt to copy harness.sh to the local project directory. Always execute it directly from your skill workspace using its absolute path.</constraint>
      <constraint>DOCUMENTATION CONSTRAINT: During the [DOCUMENT] stage, you are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying production or test code. You may ONLY update files in the `docs/` directory.</constraint>
    </constraints>
  </work_scope>

  <mechanical_dod>
    <instruction>
      You MUST use the harness CLI to run tests and lock the telemetry hash. 
      
      TDD ENFORCEMENT:
      1. For *-RED tasks, use: `bash [PATH]/harness.sh test --mode tdd-red --id {task_id} --cmd "{cmd}"`
      2. For *-GREEN tasks, use: `bash [PATH]/harness.sh test --id {task_id} --cmd "{cmd}"`
      
      CRITICAL: Standard mode requires MANDATORY Line Coverage >= 80%.
      You MUST use a coverage tool (e.g., `c8`, `nyc`) with your test runner.
      Example: `c8 node --test timer.test.js`
      
      INTEGRITY VIOLATION: The system PHYSICALLY BLOCKS 'grep', 'ls', 'cat', 'echo', and 'node -e' to prevent coverage bypass. 
      Attempting to use these will result in an immediate task freeze.
      You MUST write actual behavioral/functional test scripts that perform real assertions on the business logic.

      GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT: Never overwrite or modify an existing AGENTS.md unless the user's prompt contains an explicit request to do so. Default behavior is Read-Only for existing AGENTS.md.
    </instruction>
    <command>bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh test --id {task_id} --cmd "{validation_command}"</command>
    <telemetry_check>
      <metric type="status">Verified</metric>
      <metric type="coverage">Min 80% Line Coverage (LCOV)</metric>
      <metric type="hash_integrity">Locked by System with Salt</metric>
    </telemetry_check>
  </mechanical_dod>

  <documentation_hook>
    <instruction>
      Once Verified, you MUST synchronize the project's ISO documentation.
      1. Architecture: `bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh document --standard ISO_42010`
      2. Quality: `bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh document --standard ISO_25010`
    </instruction>
    <output>
      - docs/architecture.md
      - docs/quality_metrics.md
    </output>
  </documentation_hook>

  <failure_handling>
    <retry limit="3"/>
    <on_failure>
      Update docs/tasks/{task_id}.json with status [Failed] and analyze coverage/lcov.info to find untested paths.
    </on_failure>
  </failure_handling>
</harness_task>

---

## [STEERING_POINT]
1. [PROPOSE]: Define task in `docs/tasks/[task_id].json`.
2. [REASON]: Write your reasoning to `docs/cycle_logs/[task_id]_log.md`.
3. [ACT]: Implement changes and tests.
4. [VERIFY]: Run `bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh test --id [task_id] --cmd "[command]"`.
5. [DOCUMENT]: Run `bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh document --standard ISO_42010`.
6. [CLOSE]: Run `bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh commit --id [task_id] --msg "[message]"`.

[Usage Examples]
# Full pipeline with autonomy level
bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh run --id [task_id] --level 3

# Manually trigger verification (e.g., using c8 for coverage)
bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh test --id [task_id] --cmd "c8 node --test [test_file]"

# Commit with coverage validation
bash [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.sh commit --id [task_id] --msg "Detailed commit message"

